import Mathlib
import MassGap.ObserverCarries
import MassGap.ClayStatementG
import MassGap.FlowG

/-!
# MassGap.ObsGenFam — the observer clause on a family of flows (amendment 3 of clause 28)

`ClayStatement.ObsGen` (clause 28) asks that `X.base.H` be the closed span of the vectors of one
observer flow `W`. This module states the clause on a family of observer flows `Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N`
with `Wf 0 = W` and physical flow range tending to `0` (`ObsGenFam`, `ObsGenFamG` over `G`), proves
how it relates to `ObsGen`, and proves which degenerate cases it excludes.

## The amended clause

`ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X Wf`:

* `Wf 0 = W`, the flow of clauses 1 and 16;
* `FlowRangeToZero D hD Wf`: for every `r' > 0`, eventually in `n`, `(energy0 (Wf n) D hD)` has
  physical range `r'` (`Flow.PhysRange`, eventually in the step `a_k · range_k ≤ r'`;
  `physRange_energy0_iff`: the range of `Wf n` itself);
* vectors `v n P ∈ X.base.H` of the compact margin monomials, one family per member, with
  `v 0 Q = X.cvec Q` on the class `D`; for every `n, m, P, Q` the two-flow lattice reading
  `latSF2` of `θP ∪ Q` (`θP` flowed by `Wf n`, `Q` flowed by `Wf m`, both through `energy0`)
  converging along `ultra` to `contSF2`, and `⟪v n P, v m Q⟫ = contSF2`; the time translation by
  `a_m` acting on every member's vectors as the dyadic shift of the test functions;
* the closed span of `⋃ₙ range (v n)` is all of `X.base.H`.

`ObsGenFam = ∃ Wf, ObsGenFamWith … Wf`. At `n = m` the two-flow reading is the member's own flowed
reading (`latSF2_self`, `contSF2_self`).

## What is proved

* `obsGen_core_of_fam`: the amended clause gives every part of `ObsGen` at `W` except generation:
  `v 0` is the observer's compact vectors on `D`, has Gram matrix `S_W(θP ∪ Q)`, and the time
  translations act on it as the shifts. `hlg_zero_le`: its closed span lies inside `X.base.H`
  generated by the family.
* `obsGenFam_of_gen_zero`: if the members' vectors already have closed span `⊤` at `n = 0` (the
  generation of `ObsGen`, clause 28), the amended clause holds; generation by `W` alone implies
  generation by the family.
* `obsGenFamWith_const`: `ObsGen` at `W`, with the uniform bound of `energy0 W` and `W` itself of
  physical range below every `r' > 0`, is the amended clause at the constant family.
  `flowRangeToZero_const_iff`: the constant family meets the range condition exactly when `W` does;
  `not_flowRangeToZero_const`: at a flow without physical range `r'` for some `r' > 0` (a flow of
  fixed physical range `r > 0`) the constant family is not admitted, so the amended clause there
  asks for members other than `W`.
* `eq_zero_of_flatFamily`, `not_flatFamily`, `not_flatFlowFamily`: if every member's flowed fields
  are eventually constant, the family's joint form has rank one, `X.base.H` is a line, and the
  clauses `LinkTS` (`w ∅ = vac`, `‖vac‖ = 1`) and the non-zero vector of `HL` orthogonal to the
  vacuum cannot hold. This is the flat-flow exclusion of `ObserverCarries.not_clayData_flatFlow`
  on the family: the exclusion under `ObsGen` (clause 28) reads `W` alone; `ObsGenFam` excludes the
  family all of whose members are flat, at any `W`.
* `v_flat_line`, `obsGen_of_famFlat`: a member whose flowed fields are eventually constant has its
  vectors on the line of `v 0 E` (`E` the empty monomial); if every member `n ≠ 0` is such,
  `ObsGenFamWith` at that family gives `ObsGen` at `W`, generation included.
* `not_timeIndepFamily`: if for one `m` the joint form does not see the shift `s_m`
  (`S(θP_n ∪ s_m Q_{n'}) = S(θP_n ∪ Q_{n'})` for all members `n, n'`), `HamiltonianGap` puts every
  vector on the vacuum line, and no non-zero vector is orthogonal to the vacuum. This is
  `ObserverCarries.not_clayData_of_timeIndep` on the joint form.
* Over `G`: `ObsGenFamG`, `obsGenG_core_of_famG`, `obsGenFamG_of_gen_zero`, `obsGenFamWithG_const`.

## What `ObsGenFam` asks, against `ObsGen` (clause 28)

`ObsGen` asks one family of vectors, those of `W`, to span `X.base.H`. `ObsGenFam` asks the vectors
of every member of a family shrinking to physical range `0`, with the joint two-flow Gram matrix, to
span it, and keeps `v 0 = X.cvec` and the time covariance at every member. The directions proved:
`ObsGenFam` ⇒ `ObsGen` without generation (`obsGen_core_of_fam`); generation by `W` plus the
members' vectors ⇒ `ObsGenFam` (`obsGenFam_of_gen_zero`); `ObsGen` ⇒ `ObsGenFam` at a flow of
vanishing range (`obsGenFamWith_const`); `ObsGenFamWith` ⇒ `ObsGen` at a family whose members
`n ≠ 0` are flat (`obsGen_of_famFlat`). `ObsGenFam` asks for the members' vectors, which `ObsGen`
does not provide; `ObsGen` asks generation by `W` alone, which `ObsGenFam` does not.

The flat-flow exclusion `ObserverCarries.not_clayStatementAt_flatFlow` reads `W` alone; its
counterpart here (`not_flatFamily`) reads every member. A flat `W` with a non-flat member is not
excluded by the results of this module.

## Faithfulness (ARGUED)

Jaffe–Witten ask for a theory satisfying the Osterwalder–Schrader axioms with a mass gap, the
Hilbert space being the Osterwalder–Schrader reconstruction from the theory's Schwinger functions.
ARGUED: the Schwinger functions of the local fields are the limits of the flowed ones as the flow's
physical range tends to `0`, and the reconstruction from one flow of fixed range `r > 0` is that of
the fields smeared at scale `r`, a subspace. A family whose range tends to `0`, with the joint
(two-flow) Gram matrix, reaches the local fields only when its members' flowed fields carry them;
the range condition alone does not ask that (below). ARGUED: `ObsGenFam` states the clause's
intent (the Hilbert space is the reconstruction from the theory's own Schwinger functions) on a
space at least as large: `hlg_zero_le` (proved) puts the span of `W`'s vectors inside the span of
the family's, and the gap clause 26 is stated on `HLC`, unchanged. No OS or spectral clause is
touched by the amendment (clauses 1–27 are the same), and the clause asks the time translations to
act on every member's vectors as the shifts. `not_flatFamily` and `not_timeIndepFamily` (proved)
exclude a family all of whose members are flat, or whose joint form does not see one time step. A
flat `W` with a non-flat member is not excluded.

`FlowRangeToZero` bounds the members' reach, not their content. `ObsJoint.flowRangeToZero_flatTail`
(proved) meets it at every `W` with flat members `n ≥ 1`, and at any family whose members `n ≠ 0`
have eventually constant flowed fields, `ObsGenFamWith` implies `ObsGen` at `W`
(`obsGen_of_famFlat`, proved). The clause therefore does not force the reconstruction of the local
fields; that needs a condition on the members' content.

Foundational footprint only (`#print axioms` at the end of each declaration).

DERIVED (module-wide): `0` the first member, the empty monomial's length, the vanishing pairing and
the zero vector; `1` one step, the empty product and the norm of the vacuum; `4` in `Fin 4` the
spacetime dimension.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace MassGap.ObsFamily

open MassGap MassGap.InfiniteLattice MassGap.ContinuumField MassGap.ContinuumSchwinger
  MassGap.ContinuumFlow MassGap.ObserverOS MassGap.ObserverEnergyMoments MassGap.ObserverOSLinked
  MassGap.ObserverOSReconstructionS MassGap.ObserverSymField MassGap.ClayStatement
  MassGap.ExistenceFlow MassGap.ObserverCarries MassGap.ClayFull Filter
open scoped Topology

variable {N : ℕ}

/-! ## 1. The two-flow reading -/

section TwoFlow

/-- **The two-flow lattice reading** of step `k`: `θP` flowed by `Φ`, `Q` flowed by `Ψ`,
`ν_k(∏ᵢ smear a_k (Φ_k (θPᵢ)) · ∏ⱼ smear a_k (Ψ_k Qⱼ))`.

DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def latSF2 (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ Ψ : Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) (k : ℕ) (P Q : Mono N) : ℝ :=
  latSk hN k (Sum.elim (fun i => Φ.field k (SField.refl τ (P.2 i))) (fun j => Ψ.field k (Q.2 j)))

/-- **The two-flow reading**, the limit along `ultra`. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def contSF2 (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ Ψ : Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) (P Q : Mono N) : ℝ :=
  limUnder (ultra : Filter ℕ) (fun k => latSF2 hN Φ Ψ τ k P Q)

/-- At one flow the two-flow reading is the flowed reading of `θP ∪ Q`. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem latSF2_self (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ : Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) (k : ℕ) (P Q : Mono N) :
    latSF2 hN Φ Φ τ k P Q = latSF hN Φ k (pairFam τ P Q) := by
  unfold latSF2 latSF
  congr 1
  funext x
  cases x <;> rfl

#print axioms latSF2_self

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem contSF2_self (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ : Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) (P Q : Mono N) :
    contSF2 hN Φ Φ τ P Q = contSF hN Φ (pairFam τ P Q) := by
  unfold contSF2 contSF
  simp only [latSF2_self]

#print axioms contSF2_self

/-- **A lattice reading of constant fields is the product of one number per field.**

DERIVED: `1` the identity configuration. -/
theorem latSk_const (hN : N ≠ 0) (k : ℕ) {ι : Type} [Fintype ι] (F : ι → SField N)
    (h : ∀ i U, (F i).1.1 U = (F i).1.1 1) :
    latSk hN k F = ∏ i, smear (dySpacing N k) (F i).1.1 (F i).2 1 := by
  show stateK hN k (∏ i, smear (dySpacing N k) (F i).1.1 (F i).2) = _
  exact state_prod_const _ _ (fun i => smear_const (dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k) _
    (h i) (F i).2)

#print axioms latSk_const

/-- **The two-flow reading of constant fields factors** through the empty monomial `E`:
`S_k(θP ∪ Q) = S_k(θP ∪ E) · S_k(θE ∪ Q)`, whatever flows read the empty side.

DERIVED: `1` the empty products. -/
theorem latSF2_factor (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ Ψ Φ' Ψ' : Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ} (k : ℕ)
    (P Q : Mono N) (hP : ∀ i, CstAt Φ k (SField.refl τ (P.2 i)).1)
    (hQ : ∀ j, CstAt Ψ k (Q.2 j).1) :
    latSF2 hN Φ Ψ τ k P Q
      = latSF2 hN Φ Ψ' τ k P (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1
        * latSF2 hN Φ' Ψ τ k (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1 Q := by
  haveI : IsEmpty (Fin (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1.1) := by
    show IsEmpty (Fin 0)
    infer_instance
  unfold latSF2
  rw [latSk_const hN k _ (fun x => by
        cases x with
        | inl i => exact hP i
        | inr j => exact hQ j),
    latSk_const hN k _ (fun x => by
        cases x with
        | inl i => exact hP i
        | inr j => exact isEmptyElim j),
    latSk_const hN k _ (fun x => by
        cases x with
        | inl i => exact isEmptyElim i
        | inr j => exact hQ j)]
  rw [Fintype.prod_sum_type, Fintype.prod_sum_type, Fintype.prod_sum_type,
    Fintype.prod_empty (ι := Fin (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1.1),
    Fintype.prod_empty (ι := Fin (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1.1), mul_one, one_mul]
  try rfl

#print axioms latSF2_factor

/-- **`S(θE ∪ E) = 1`** at any two flows. DERIVED: `1` the value. -/
theorem contSF2_empty (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ Ψ : Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ} :
    contSF2 hN Φ Ψ τ (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1 (emptyM τ r).1 = 1 := by
  haveI : ((ultra : Ultrafilter ℕ) : Filter ℕ).NeBot := ultra.neBot'
  have e : (fun k => latSF2 hN Φ Ψ τ k (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1 (emptyM τ r).1)
      = fun _ => (1 : ℝ) := by
    funext k
    haveI : IsEmpty (Fin (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1.1 ⊕ Fin (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1.1) := by
      show IsEmpty (Fin 0 ⊕ Fin 0)
      infer_instance
    show stateK hN k (∏ i, smear _ _ _) = 1
    rw [Fintype.prod_empty]
    exact MassGap.DLRLimit.State.map_one _
  unfold contSF2
  rw [e]
  exact tendsto_const_nhds.limUnder_eq

#print axioms contSF2_empty

end TwoFlow

/-! ## 2. The amended clause -/

section Clause

variable {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))} {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ}

/-- **The physical range of `energy0 W` is that of `W`.** DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem physRange_energy0_iff (W : ConfFlow N) (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D) (r : ℝ) :
    (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r ↔ ∀ᶠ k in atTop, dySpacing N k * (W.range k : ℝ) ≤ r :=
  Iff.rfl

#print axioms physRange_energy0_iff

/-- **The physical flow range tends to `0`**: for every `r' > 0`, eventually in `n`, the member
`Wf n` has physical range `r'` (`Flow.PhysRange` of `energy0 (Wf n) D hD`).

DERIVED: `0` the limit and the sign. -/
def FlowRangeToZero (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) : Prop :=
  ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → ∀ᶠ n in atTop, (energy0 (Wf n) D hD).PhysRange r'

/-- **The vectors of a family of observers**: `v 0` the observer's compact vectors on `D`; the
two-flow readings converging along `ultra` with `⟪v n P, v m Q⟫ = contSF2`; the time translation by
`a_m` acting on every member's vectors as the dyadic shift.

DERIVED: `0` the first member; `1` one step. -/
def ObsFamV (hN : N ≠ 0) (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) (v : ℕ → MarginMono N τ r → X.base.H) :
    Prop :=
  (∀ Q : MarginMonoD N D τ r, v 0 Q.1 = X.cvec Q)
    ∧ (∀ (n m : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMono N τ r),
      Tendsto (fun k => latSF2 hN (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) (energy0 (Wf m) D hD) τ k P.1 Q.1)
          (ultra : Filter ℕ) (𝓝 (contSF2 hN (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) (energy0 (Wf m) D hD) τ P.1 Q.1))
        ∧ inner ℂ (v n P) (v m Q)
          = (contSF2 hN (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) (energy0 (Wf m) D hD) τ P.1 Q.1 : ℂ))
    ∧ (∀ (n m : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMono N τ r),
      Q.1 = ⟨P.1.1, fun i => ((P.1.2 i).1, (P.1.2 i).2.translate (timeVec N m τ 1))⟩ →
        v n Q = X.base.time (dySpacing N m) (v n P))

/-- **The amended clause 28 at a family `Wf`**: `Wf 0 = W`, physical flow range tending to `0`,
the members' vectors (`ObsFamV`), and the closed span of all of them the whole space.

DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
def ObsGenFamWith (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) : Prop :=
  Wf 0 = W ∧ FlowRangeToZero D hD Wf
    ∧ ∃ v : ℕ → MarginMono N τ r → X.base.H, ObsFamV hN D hD X Wf v
      ∧ HLg X.base (fun p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r => v p.1 p.2) = ⊤

/-- **The amended clause 28**: the observer's reconstruction space is generated by a family of
observer flows with `Wf 0 = W` and physical flow range tending to `0`.

DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def ObsGenFam (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) : Prop :=
  ∃ Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N, ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X Wf

/-- **The span of the first member lies in the span of the family.** DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem hlg_zero_le (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (v : ℕ → MarginMono N τ r → X.base.H) :
    HLg X.base (v 0) ≤ HLg X.base (fun p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r => v p.1 p.2) := by
  refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_mono (Submodule.span_mono ?_)
  rintro _ ⟨P, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨(0, P), rfl⟩

#print axioms hlg_zero_le

/-- **The amended clause gives `ObsGen` at `W` without its generation**: `v 0` is the observer's
compact vectors on `D`, with Gram matrix `S_W(θP ∪ Q)`, and the time translations act on it as the
shifts.

DERIVED: `0` the first member; `1` one step. -/
theorem obsGen_core_of_fam (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (h : ObsGenFam hN W D hD X) :
    ∃ v : MarginMono N τ r → X.base.H,
      (∀ Q : MarginMonoD N D τ r, v Q.1 = X.cvec Q)
      ∧ (∀ P Q : MarginMono N τ r,
        inner ℂ (v P) (v Q) = (contSF hN (energy0 W D hD) (pairFam τ P.1 Q.1) : ℂ))
      ∧ (∀ (m : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMono N τ r),
        Q.1 = ⟨P.1.1, fun i => ((P.1.2 i).1, (P.1.2 i).2.translate (timeVec N m τ 1))⟩ →
          v Q = X.base.time (dySpacing N m) (v P)) := by
  obtain ⟨Wf, h0, -, v, ⟨hc, hG, hT⟩, -⟩ := h
  subst h0
  exact ⟨v 0, hc, fun P Q => by rw [(hG 0 0 P Q).2, contSF2_self],
    fun m P Q hQ => hT 0 m P Q hQ⟩

#print axioms obsGen_core_of_fam

/-- **Generation by the first member implies generation by the family.**

DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem obsGenFam_of_gen_zero (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) (h0 : Wf 0 = W)
    (hR : FlowRangeToZero D hD Wf) (v : ℕ → MarginMono N τ r → X.base.H)
    (hv : ObsFamV hN D hD X Wf v) (hgen : HLg X.base (v 0) = ⊤) :
    ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X Wf :=
  ⟨h0, hR, v, hv, top_le_iff.mp (hgen ▸ hlg_zero_le X v)⟩

#print axioms obsGenFam_of_gen_zero

/-- **`ObsGen` at a flow of vanishing physical range is the amended clause at the constant family.**
With `UniformBoundF` of `energy0 W` (the convergence half of `ApertureConv`) and `W` of physical
range below every `r' > 0`, `ObsGen` at `W` gives `ObsGenFamWith` at `fun _ => W`.

DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem obsGenFamWith_const (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (hB : UniformBoundF hN (energy0 W D hD))
    (hR : ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r') (h : ObsGen hN W D hD X) :
    ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X (fun _ => W) := by
  obtain ⟨v, hc, hG, hT, hgen⟩ := h
  have hrange : Set.range (fun p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r => v p.2) = Set.range v := by
    ext x
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨⟨_, P⟩, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨P, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨P, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨(0, P), rfl⟩
  refine ⟨rfl, fun r' hr' => Filter.Eventually.of_forall (fun _ => hR r' hr'), fun _ => v,
    ⟨hc, fun n m P Q => ⟨?_, ?_⟩, fun n m P Q hQ => hT m P Q hQ⟩, ?_⟩
  · simp only [latSF2_self, contSF2_self]
    exact tendsto_contSF hN _ hB _
  · rw [contSF2_self]
    exact hG P Q
  · show (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (fun p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r => v p.2))).topologicalClosure
      = ⊤
    rw [hrange]
    exact hgen

#print axioms obsGenFamWith_const

/-- **The constant family meets the range condition exactly when `W` does.**

DERIVED: `0` the sign. -/
theorem flowRangeToZero_const_iff (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D) :
    FlowRangeToZero D hD (fun _ => W) ↔ ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r' := by
  constructor
  · intro h r' hr'
    obtain ⟨_, hn⟩ := (h r' hr').exists
    exact hn
  · intro h r' hr'
    exact Filter.Eventually.of_forall (fun _ => h r' hr')

#print axioms flowRangeToZero_const_iff

/-- **At a flow without physical range `r'` for some `r' > 0`, the constant family is not
admitted.**

DERIVED: `0` the sign. -/
theorem not_flowRangeToZero_const (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D) {r' : ℝ}
    (hr' : 0 < r') (h : ¬ (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r') :
    ¬ FlowRangeToZero D hD (fun _ => W) :=
  fun hR => h ((flowRangeToZero_const_iff W hD).mp hR r' hr')

#print axioms not_flowRangeToZero_const

end Clause

/-! ## 3. Flat members: no witness at an all-flat family, `ObsGen` at a flat tail -/

section Flat

variable {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))} {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ}

/-- **The joint form of a flat family has rank one.** If every member's flowed fields are eventually
constant, the family's vectors span a line: every vector orthogonal to a non-zero vector is `0`.

DERIVED: `0` the first member, the vanishing pairing and the zero vector. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_flatFamily (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) (hfam : ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X Wf)
    (hC : ∀ (n : ℕ) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)),
      ∀ᶠ k in atTop, CstAt (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) k O)
    {x : X.base.H} (hx : x ≠ 0) {u : X.base.H} (hu : inner ℂ x u = 0) : u = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨-, -, v, ⟨-, hG, -⟩, hgen⟩ := hfam
  set Φ : ℕ → Flow N := fun n => energy0 (Wf n) D hD
  set E : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r := (0, emptyM τ r)
  refine eq_zero_of_rankOne (fun p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r => v p.1 p.2) E
    (fun p q => contSF2 hN (Φ p.1) (Φ q.1) τ p.2.1 q.2.1) (fun p q => (hG p.1 q.1 p.2 q.2).2)
    (fun p q => ?_) (contSF2_empty hN _ _ τ) hgen hx hu
  obtain ⟨n, P⟩ := p
  obtain ⟨m, Q⟩ := q
  have hev : ∀ᶠ k in atTop, latSF2 hN (Φ n) (Φ m) τ k P.1 Q.1
      = latSF2 hN (Φ n) (Φ 0) τ k P.1 (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1
        * latSF2 hN (Φ 0) (Φ m) τ k (emptyM (N := N) τ r).1 Q.1 := by
    filter_upwards [Filter.eventually_all.2 (fun i => hC n (SField.refl τ (P.1.2 i)).1),
      Filter.eventually_all.2 (fun j => hC m (Q.1.2 j).1)] with k hP hQ
    exact latSF2_factor hN (Φ n) (Φ m) (Φ 0) (Φ 0) τ k P.1 Q.1 hP hQ
  have h2 := (hG n 0 P (emptyM τ r)).1.mul (hG 0 m (emptyM τ r) Q).1
  exact tendsto_nhds_unique (hG n m P Q).1
    (h2.congr' (EventuallyEq.symm (hev.filter_mono ultra_le)))

#print axioms eq_zero_of_flatFamily

/-- **No witness at a flat family.** With `LinkTS` (`w ∅ = vac`, `⟪w ∅, w ∅⟫ = 1`, so `vac ≠ 0`) and
a non-zero vector of `HL` orthogonal to the vacuum (clause 12), the amended clause 28 cannot be met
by a family all of whose members' flowed fields are eventually constant.

DERIVED: `0` the vanishing pairing and the zero vector; `1` the norm of the vacuum. -/
theorem not_flatFamily (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (ρ : RenormMix N) (w : TSep τ → X.base.H)
    (hLT : LinkTS hN W D hD X ρ w) (hnt : ∃ u ∈ HLs X w, inner ℂ X.base.vac u = 0 ∧ u ≠ 0)
    (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) (hfam : ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X Wf)
    (hC : ∀ (n : ℕ) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)),
      ∀ᶠ k in atTop, CstAt (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) k O) : False := by
  have hvac : X.base.vac ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    have h1 := (hLT.1 (emptyT τ) (emptyT τ)).2
    rw [hLT.2.2.1, h0, inner_zero_left, kernT_empty] at h1
    norm_num at h1
  obtain ⟨u, -, hu0, hune⟩ := hnt
  exact hune (eq_zero_of_flatFamily hN W hD X Wf hfam hC hvac hu0)

#print axioms not_flatFamily

/-- **No witness at a family of flat flows** `Wf n = flatFlow (L n)`, `L n k → ∞` in `k` for each
`n`.

DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem not_flatFlowFamily (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (ρ : RenormMix N) (w : TSep τ → X.base.H)
    (hLT : LinkTS hN W D hD X ρ w) (hnt : ∃ u ∈ HLs X w, inner ℂ X.base.vac u = 0 ∧ u ≠ 0)
    {L : ℕ → ℕ → ℕ} (hL : ∀ n, Tendsto (L n) atTop atTop)
    (hfam : ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X (fun n => flatFlow (N := N) (L n))) : False :=
  not_flatFamily hN W hD X ρ w hLT hnt _ hfam (fun n O => energy0_flat_const (hL n) D hD O)

#print axioms not_flatFlowFamily

/-- **A flat member's vectors lie on one line.** If member `n`'s flowed fields are eventually
constant, `v n P = S(θP_n ∪ E_0) · v 0 E`, `E` the empty monomial: `S(θP_n ∪ P_n)` factors as
`S(θP_n ∪ E_0) · S(θE_0 ∪ P_n)` (`latSF2_factor`), so `v n P − c · v 0 E` has norm `0`.

DERIVED: `0` the first member and the zero vector; `1` the norm of `v 0 E`. -/
theorem v_flat_line (hN : N ≠ 0)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) (v : ℕ → MarginMono N τ r → X.base.H)
    (hv : ObsFamV hN D hD X Wf v) (n : ℕ)
    (hC : ∀ O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N), ∀ᶠ k in atTop, CstAt (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) k O)
    (P : MarginMono N τ r) :
    v n P = ((contSF2 hN (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) (energy0 (Wf 0) D hD) τ P.1 (emptyM τ r).1 : ℝ) : ℂ)
      • v 0 (emptyM τ r) := by
  haveI : ((ultra : Ultrafilter ℕ) : Filter ℕ).NeBot := ultra.neBot'
  obtain ⟨-, hG, -⟩ := hv
  set Φ : ℕ → Flow N := fun n => energy0 (Wf n) D hD
  set E : MarginMono N τ r := emptyM τ r
  have hev : ∀ᶠ k in atTop, latSF2 hN (Φ n) (Φ n) τ k P.1 P.1
      = latSF2 hN (Φ n) (Φ 0) τ k P.1 E.1 * latSF2 hN (Φ 0) (Φ n) τ k E.1 P.1 := by
    filter_upwards [Filter.eventually_all.2 (fun i => hC (SField.refl τ (P.1.2 i)).1),
      Filter.eventually_all.2 (fun j => hC (P.1.2 j).1)] with k hP hQ
    exact latSF2_factor hN (Φ n) (Φ n) (Φ 0) (Φ 0) τ (r := r) k P.1 P.1 hP hQ
  have hpp : contSF2 hN (Φ n) (Φ n) τ P.1 P.1
      = contSF2 hN (Φ n) (Φ 0) τ P.1 E.1 * contSF2 hN (Φ 0) (Φ n) τ E.1 P.1 :=
    tendsto_nhds_unique (hG n n P P).1
      (((hG n 0 P E).1.mul (hG 0 n E P).1).congr' (EventuallyEq.symm (hev.filter_mono ultra_le)))
  set c : ℝ := contSF2 hN (Φ n) (Φ 0) τ P.1 E.1
  have hc' : contSF2 hN (Φ 0) (Φ n) τ E.1 P.1 = c := by
    have h1 := (hG 0 n E P).2
    rw [← inner_conj_symm, (hG n 0 P E).2, Complex.conj_ofReal] at h1
    exact_mod_cast h1.symm
  have hee : contSF2 hN (Φ 0) (Φ 0) τ E.1 E.1 = 1 := contSF2_empty hN _ _ τ
  have hd : inner ℂ (v n P - (c : ℂ) • v 0 E) (v n P - (c : ℂ) • v 0 E) = 0 := by
    simp only [inner_sub_left, inner_sub_right, inner_smul_left, inner_smul_right]
    rw [(hG n n P P).2, (hG n 0 P E).2, (hG 0 n E P).2, (hG 0 0 E E).2, hpp, hc', hee,
      Complex.conj_ofReal]
    push_cast
    ring
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (inner_self_eq_zero.mp hd)

#print axioms v_flat_line

/-- **At a family whose members `n ≠ 0` are flat, `ObsGenFamWith` gives `ObsGen` at `W`**,
generation included: every flat member's vectors are multiples of `v 0 E` (`v_flat_line`), so the
family's span is the span of `v 0`. No `UniformBoundF` enters.

DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem obsGen_of_famFlat (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) (h : ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X Wf)
    (hC : ∀ n : ℕ, n ≠ 0 → ∀ O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N), ∀ᶠ k in atTop,
      CstAt (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) k O) :
    ObsGen hN W D hD X := by
  obtain ⟨h0, -, v, hv, hgen⟩ := h
  subst h0
  obtain ⟨hc, hG, hT⟩ := hv
  set S := Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (v 0))
  have hmem : ∀ p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r, v p.1 p.2 ∈ S := by
    rintro ⟨n, P⟩
    by_cases hn : n = 0
    · subst hn
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨P, rfl⟩
    · rw [v_flat_line hN hD X Wf v ⟨hc, hG, hT⟩ n (hC n hn) P]
      exact S.smul_mem _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, rfl⟩)
  refine ⟨v 0, hc, fun P Q => by rw [(hG 0 0 P Q).2, contSF2_self],
    fun m P Q hQ => hT 0 m P Q hQ, ?_⟩
  refine top_le_iff.mp ?_
  rw [← hgen]
  refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_mono (Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_)
  rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩
  exact hmem p

#print axioms obsGen_of_famFlat

end Flat

/-! ## 4. A family whose joint form does not see time carries no witness -/

section TimeIndep

variable {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))} {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ}

/-- **No witness when the joint form does not see one time step.** If for one `m`
`S(θP_n ∪ s_m Q_{n'}) = S(θP_n ∪ Q_{n'})` for all members `n, n'` and margin monomials, the time
covariance of the amended clause makes `X.base.time (a_m)` fix every member's vectors, hence all of
`X.base.H`; the last clause of `HamiltonianGap` puts every vector on the vacuum line, and no non-zero
vector is orthogonal to the vacuum.

DERIVED: `0` the vanishing pairing, the zero vector and the sign of `a_m`. -/
theorem not_timeIndepFamily (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (hH : HamiltonianGap X.base)
    (hnt : ∃ u : X.base.H, inner ℂ X.base.vac u = 0 ∧ u ≠ 0)
    (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlow N) (hfam : ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X Wf) (m : ℕ)
    (hti : ∀ (n n' : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMono N τ r),
      contSF2 hN (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) (energy0 (Wf n') D hD) τ P.1
          (MarginMono.shift hN τ m Q).1
        = contSF2 hN (energy0 (Wf n) D hD) (energy0 (Wf n') D hD) τ P.1 Q.1) : False := by
  obtain ⟨-, -, v, ⟨-, hG, hT⟩, hgen'⟩ := hfam
  set vv : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r → X.base.H := fun p => v p.1 p.2
  have hgen : (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range vv)).topologicalClosure = ⊤ := hgen'
  have hfix : ∀ (n : ℕ) (Q : MarginMono N τ r), v n (MarginMono.shift hN τ m Q) = v n Q := by
    intro n Q
    set d := v n (MarginMono.shift hN τ m Q) - v n Q
    have hle : Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range vv) ≤ (ℂ ∙ d)ᗮ := by
      rw [Submodule.span_le]
      rintro _ ⟨⟨n', P⟩, rfl⟩
      rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Submodule.mem_orthogonal_singleton_iff_inner_right,
        inner_eq_zero_symm]
      show inner ℂ (v n' P) (v n (MarginMono.shift hN τ m Q) - v n Q) = 0
      rw [inner_sub_right, (hG n' n P _).2, (hG n' n P Q).2, hti n' n P Q, sub_self]
    have htop : (⊤ : Submodule ℂ X.base.H) ≤ (ℂ ∙ d)ᗮ := by
      have h1 := Submodule.topologicalClosure_mono hle
      rw [(Submodule.isClosed_orthogonal (ℂ ∙ d)).submodule_topologicalClosure_eq, hgen] at h1
      exact h1
    have hd := htop (Submodule.mem_top (x := d))
    rw [Submodule.mem_orthogonal_singleton_iff_inner_right, inner_self_eq_zero] at hd
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp hd
  have hker : ∀ x : X.base.H, X.base.time (dySpacing N m) x = x := by
    let T : X.base.H →L[ℂ] X.base.H :=
      X.base.time (dySpacing N m) - ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ X.base.H
    let K : Submodule ℂ X.base.H := LinearMap.ker (T : X.base.H →ₗ[ℂ] X.base.H)
    have hmem : ∀ x, x ∈ K ↔ X.base.time (dySpacing N m) x = x := by
      intro x
      show T x = 0 ↔ _
      show X.base.time (dySpacing N m) x - x = 0 ↔ _
      exact sub_eq_zero
    have hle : Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range vv) ≤ K := by
      rw [Submodule.span_le]
      rintro _ ⟨⟨n, Q⟩, rfl⟩
      rw [SetLike.mem_coe, hmem]
      show X.base.time (dySpacing N m) (v n Q) = v n Q
      rw [← hT n m Q (MarginMono.shift hN τ m Q) rfl, hfix n Q]
    have hcl : IsClosed (K : Set X.base.H) := ContinuousLinearMap.isClosed_ker T
    have h1 := Submodule.topologicalClosure_mono hle
    rw [hcl.submodule_topologicalClosure_eq, hgen] at h1
    intro x
    exact (hmem x).mp (h1 (Submodule.mem_top (x := x)))
  obtain ⟨u, hu0, hune⟩ := hnt
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hH.2.2.2.2 (dySpacing N m) (dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) m) u
    (hker u)
  have hvac : X.base.vac ≠ 0 := by
    rintro h0
    exact hune (by rw [hc, h0, smul_zero])
  rw [hc, inner_smul_right] at hu0
  have hvv : inner ℂ X.base.vac X.base.vac ≠ 0 := inner_self_ne_zero.mpr hvac
  have c0 : c = 0 := (mul_eq_zero.mp hu0).resolve_right hvv
  exact hune (by rw [hc, c0, zero_smul])

#print axioms not_timeIndepFamily

end TimeIndep

/-! ## 5. Over `G` -/

section OverG

open MassGap.ClayTreeG MassGap.ClayStatementG

variable {G : Type} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [MeasurableSpace G] [GaugeGroup G]
  {D : Set (LField G)} {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ}

/-- **The two-flow lattice reading over `G`**. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def latSF2G (S : Sched G) (Φ Ψ : ℕ → LField G → LField G) (τ : Fin 4) (k : ℕ) (P Q : MonoG G) :
    ℝ :=
  latSG S k (Sum.elim (fun i => (Φ k ((P.2 i).1.refl τ), (P.2 i).2.reflect τ))
    (fun j => (Ψ k (Q.2 j).1, (Q.2 j).2)))

/-- The two-flow reading over `G`, the limit along `ultra`. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def contSF2G (S : Sched G) (Φ Ψ : ℕ → LField G → LField G) (τ : Fin 4) (P Q : MonoG G) : ℝ :=
  limUnder (ultra : Filter ℕ) (fun k => latSF2G S Φ Ψ τ k P Q)

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem latSF2G_self (S : Sched G) (Φ : ℕ → LField G → LField G) (τ : Fin 4) (k : ℕ)
    (P Q : MonoG G) :
    latSF2G S Φ Φ τ k P Q
      = latSFG S Φ k (Sum.elim (fun i => ((P.2 i).1.refl τ, (P.2 i).2.reflect τ)) Q.2) := by
  unfold latSF2G latSFG
  congr 1
  funext x
  cases x <;> rfl

#print axioms latSF2G_self

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem contSF2G_self (S : Sched G) (Φ : ℕ → LField G → LField G) (τ : Fin 4) (P Q : MonoG G) :
    contSF2G S Φ Φ τ P Q
      = contSFG S Φ (Sum.elim (fun i => ((P.2 i).1.refl τ, (P.2 i).2.reflect τ)) Q.2) := by
  unfold contSF2G contSFG
  simp only [latSF2G_self]

#print axioms contSF2G_self

/-- **The physical flow range tends to `0` over the schedule `S`** (`FlowG.GFlow.PhysRange` of the
members, `S.a k · range_k ≤ r'` eventually in `k`). DERIVED: `0` the limit and the sign. -/
def FlowRangeToZeroG (S : Sched G) (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlowG G) : Prop :=
  ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → ∀ᶠ n in atTop, ∀ᶠ k in atTop, S.a k * ((Wf n).range k : ℝ) ≤ r'

/-- **The vectors of a family of observers over `G`.** DERIVED: `0` the first member; `1` one step. -/
def ObsFamVG (S : Sched G) (D : Set (LField G)) (X : OSDataSLinkedG G D τ r)
    (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlowG G) (v : ℕ → MarginMonoG G τ r → X.base.H) : Prop :=
  (∀ Q : MarginMonoDG G D τ r, v 0 Q.1 = X.cvec Q)
    ∧ (∀ (n m : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMonoG G τ r),
      Tendsto (fun k => latSF2G S (energyMapG S (Wf n) D) (energyMapG S (Wf m) D) τ k P.1 Q.1)
          (ultra : Filter ℕ)
          (𝓝 (contSF2G S (energyMapG S (Wf n) D) (energyMapG S (Wf m) D) τ P.1 Q.1))
        ∧ inner ℂ (v n P) (v m Q)
          = (contSF2G S (energyMapG S (Wf n) D) (energyMapG S (Wf m) D) τ P.1 Q.1 : ℂ))
    ∧ (∀ (n m : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMonoG G τ r),
      Q.1 = ⟨P.1.1, fun i => ((P.1.2 i).1, (P.1.2 i).2.translate (timeVecG S m τ 1))⟩ →
        v n Q = X.base.time (S.a m) (v n P))

/-- **The amended clause 28 over `G` at a family `Wf`.** DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
def ObsGenFamWithG (S : Sched G) (W : ConfFlowG G) (D : Set (LField G))
    (X : OSDataSLinkedG G D τ r) (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlowG G) : Prop :=
  Wf 0 = W ∧ FlowRangeToZeroG S Wf
    ∧ ∃ v : ℕ → MarginMonoG G τ r → X.base.H, ObsFamVG S D X Wf v
      ∧ HLg X.base (fun p : ℕ × MarginMonoG G τ r => v p.1 p.2) = ⊤

/-- **The amended clause 28 over `G`.** DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def ObsGenFamG (S : Sched G) (W : ConfFlowG G) (D : Set (LField G)) (X : OSDataSLinkedG G D τ r) :
    Prop :=
  ∃ Wf : ℕ → ConfFlowG G, ObsGenFamWithG S W D X Wf

/-- **`ObsGenG` without its generation, from the amended clause.**

DERIVED: `0` the first member; `1` one step. -/
theorem obsGenG_core_of_famG (S : Sched G) (W : ConfFlowG G) (X : OSDataSLinkedG G D τ r)
    (h : ObsGenFamG S W D X) :
    ∃ v : MarginMonoG G τ r → X.base.H,
      (∀ Q : MarginMonoDG G D τ r, v Q.1 = X.cvec Q)
      ∧ (∀ P Q : MarginMonoG G τ r,
        inner ℂ (v P) (v Q) = (contSFG S (energyMapG S W D)
          (Sum.elim (fun i => ((P.1.2 i).1.refl τ, (P.1.2 i).2.reflect τ)) Q.1.2) : ℂ))
      ∧ (∀ (m : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMonoG G τ r),
        Q.1 = ⟨P.1.1, fun i => ((P.1.2 i).1, (P.1.2 i).2.translate (timeVecG S m τ 1))⟩ →
          v Q = X.base.time (S.a m) (v P)) := by
  obtain ⟨Wf, h0, -, v, ⟨hc, hG, hT⟩, -⟩ := h
  subst h0
  exact ⟨v 0, hc, fun P Q => by rw [(hG 0 0 P Q).2, contSF2G_self],
    fun m P Q hQ => hT 0 m P Q hQ⟩

#print axioms obsGenG_core_of_famG

/-- **Generation by the first member implies generation by the family**, over `G`.

DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem obsGenFamG_of_gen_zero (S : Sched G) (W : ConfFlowG G) (X : OSDataSLinkedG G D τ r)
    (Wf : ℕ → ConfFlowG G) (h0 : Wf 0 = W) (hR : FlowRangeToZeroG S Wf)
    (v : ℕ → MarginMonoG G τ r → X.base.H) (hv : ObsFamVG S D X Wf v)
    (hgen : HLg X.base (v 0) = ⊤) : ObsGenFamWithG S W D X Wf := by
  refine ⟨h0, hR, v, hv, top_le_iff.mp (hgen ▸ ?_)⟩
  refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_mono (Submodule.span_mono ?_)
  rintro _ ⟨P, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨(0, P), rfl⟩

#print axioms obsGenFamG_of_gen_zero

/-- **`ObsGenG` at a flow of vanishing physical range is the amended clause at the constant
family**, over `G`.

DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem obsGenFamWithG_const (S : Sched G) (W : ConfFlowG G) (X : OSDataSLinkedG G D τ r)
    (hB : UniformBoundFG S (energyMapG S W D))
    (hR : ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → ∀ᶠ k in atTop, S.a k * (W.range k : ℝ) ≤ r')
    (h : ObsGenG S W D X) : ObsGenFamWithG S W D X (fun _ => W) := by
  obtain ⟨v, hc, hG, hT, hgen⟩ := h
  have hrange : Set.range (fun p : ℕ × MarginMonoG G τ r => v p.2) = Set.range v := by
    ext x
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨⟨_, P⟩, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨P, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨P, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨(0, P), rfl⟩
  refine ⟨rfl, fun r' hr' => Filter.Eventually.of_forall (fun _ => hR r' hr'), fun _ => v,
    ⟨hc, fun n m P Q => ⟨?_, ?_⟩, fun n m P Q hQ => hT m P Q hQ⟩, ?_⟩
  · simp only [latSF2G_self, contSF2G_self]
    exact MassGap.FlowG.tendsto_contSFG S _ hB _
  · rw [contSF2G_self]
    exact hG P Q
  · show (Submodule.span ℂ
        (Set.range (fun p : ℕ × MarginMonoG G τ r => v p.2))).topologicalClosure = ⊤
    rw [hrange]
    exact hgen

#print axioms obsGenFamWithG_const

end OverG

